  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Stage IA right breast cancer one year after diagnosis, on adjuvant tamoxifen (C50.411)</content>. No evidence of recurrence on history, examination, or mammogram. [S]<list><item>Written survivorship care plan given today: treatment summary, surveillance schedule, possible late effects of tamoxifen, and whom to call.</item><item>Continue tamoxifen 20 mg daily.</item><item>History and examination every three to six months to year three; next left mammogram in a year.</item><item>Yearly gynecologic assessment and flu vaccine at the preventive visit next month.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Tamoxifen side effects: mild hot flashes (Z79.810)</content>. Stable and tolerable. [S]<list><item>Continue non-drug measures.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Cancer-related history and physical examination</td><td>Every 3 to 6 months for the first 3 years</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No symptoms or signs of recurrence</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Tamoxifen adherence and side effects</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taken daily for eleven months</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Vasomotor symptom assessment</td><td>Periodically on endocrine therapy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One or two mild hot flashes a day</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Abnormal vaginal bleeding inquiry on tamoxifen</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Regular periods; no intermenstrual bleeding; yearly gynecologic assessment booked for the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Venous thromboembolism symptom inquiry on tamoxifen</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No leg swelling, calf pain, or breathlessness</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Diagnostic mammogram of the left breast</td><td>Yearly after mastectomy</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done a week ago: BI-RADS 1; next in one year</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Lymphedema assessment and risk-reduction counseling</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No swelling; arm circumferences equal</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>At periodic intervals</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Fatigue, cognitive concerns, and sexual or vaginal symptoms</td><td>At each visit or periodically</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None reported</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Routine blood counts, chemistry, liver tests, and tumor markers (CEA, CA 15-3, CA 27.29)</td><td>Not recommended in asymptomatic stage I to III survivors</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No symptoms to prompt testing; none ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT, bone scan, PET, or other imaging for distant spread</td><td>Not recommended in asymptomatic survivors</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No symptoms; not ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Every 2 years on an aromatase inhibitor, on tamoxifen with ovarian suppression, or after chemotherapy-induced menopause</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Premenopausal on tamoxifen alone; bone health by diet, vitamin D, and weight-bearing exercise</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Genetic counseling</td><td>Once</td><td>Referred</td><td>Appointment next week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Survivorship care plan</td><td>Within one year of completing primary treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Written plan given and copied to medical oncology</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Healthy lifestyle counseling and second-cancer screening</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walking about 200 minutes a week; cervical and colorectal screening to be addressed at the preventive visit next month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Continue tamoxifen daily with side effects she finds tolerable. Outcome by 1979-09-28: Taking it daily; mild hot flashes controlled without medicine; no abnormal bleeding or clot symptoms [S]</item><item>Complete the yearly surveillance mammogram of the left breast. Outcome by 1979-09-28: Left mammogram one year after diagnosis: BI-RADS 1 [S]</item><item>Complete germline genetic assessment, missed at diagnosis. In progress; target 1979-10-19 [S]</item><item>Keep at least 150 minutes of activity a week and a stable weight. Outcome by 1979-09-28: Walking about 200 minutes a week; weight stable at 71 to 72 kg [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: American Cancer Society/American Society of Clinical Oncology Breast Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline. CA Cancer J Clin 2016;66(1):43-73 (2016); Breast Cancer Follow-Up and Management After Primary Treatment: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline Update. J Clin Oncol 2013;31(7):961-965 (2013); Adjuvant Endocrine Therapy for Women With Hormone Receptor-Positive Breast Cancer: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline Focused Update (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Genetic counseling next week. Adult preventive visit next month. Survivorship visit in January. Next scheduled visit 1979-10-19: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
